  "notes": "Values from the official Liebherr metric datasheet (p.11: 360°, 12.8 t). All 12 boom lengths stored. The 10.3 m boom has an over-rear '*' sub-column (60 t at 2.1 m = headline rating, 2.1-2.5 m rows only exist there) which is NOT stored. Outrigger span not printed on the table (icon only); longitudinal 7.359 m from the lower top-view chain (upper chain shows 7.341 m), transverse 6.298 m max (VarioBase 2.318-6.298 m). Max supporting force 445 kN (46 t), p.8. Operating weight not stated: jobsite driving with 12.8 t counterweight ≤ 46 t; on-road ≤ 36 t with 4.9/5.5 t (p.7). maxHookHeight not taken (graph only). The boom head overhangs the carrier front; overall length 11.976 m incl. a lightly drawn rear item (11.530 m without). Tail radius R = 3540 mm. Dims from the side/top dimension drawing: overallLength_m = carrier length (bottom dimension chain, carrier front to rear); axle positions and slew centre are cumulative sums of that chain, measured from the carrier front. Height/width = columns A/B-or-C of the dimension table for the standard 385/95 R 25 (14.00 R 25) tyres. wheelDiameter_m is NOT from the drawing: nominal value computed from the tyre designation (25 in rim + 2 x 95% x 385 mm = 1.37 m). Boom pivot height/offset are not dimensioned on the drawing (null). Liebherr remarks: hook block weight is part of the load (chartIncludesHookBlock true)."
